 * Prefix index over Unicode strings.
 *
 * Stores words in a real trie: one node per distinct prefix, walked by
 * Unicode code point so that a character outside the basic multilingual
 * plane is a single step rather than a pair of surrogate halves. Every
 * listing is ordered by code point. Each node keeps a running count of the
 * words stored below it so that `countPrefix` costs only the length of the
 * prefix.
